{
 "id": "ls20_percell",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "shape_decode_loop"
 ],
 "area": "retina",
 "description": "ls20 PER-CELL live mechanic (block 222000): the richer model that attacks 221000's trivially-converging aggregate-count residual. Each ACTION carries a Hypothesis{key, region_colour, gen, k, dr, dc, subst} -- the full 217000 Transform{dim,delta} the agent DISCOVERED by sd-loop recognition of the observed object before->after, plus the region-selector (object colour). pc_probe_pick routes to the least-observed action (Argmin visits, NO win term); pc_predict/pc_mint/pc_confirm/pc_revise grow the model by predict-and-residual. The adapter applies the graph-held Transform to the CURRENT frame to predict the per-cell next frame; the residual is scored on the CHANGE-SET (which cells change to what value), NEVER raw accuracy. NO action->transform table -- the map is minted from observation. Guarded on percell_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical otherwise), the arm, and the tick phase. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses the existing shape_decode_loop.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "ls20_percell",
  "description": "Predict WHICH cells change and to WHAT value: action x current-frame -> per-cell next-frame. The mechanic is a discovered per-action Transform applied to the current frame; surprise is the per-cell change-set residual."
 },
